.SH NAME
anpu-bench - Measure ANPU against the planted-signal fixture


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu bench [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the honesty benchmark: scan a target with each profile, match
findings against planted ground-truth signals, and report hits, misses,
and unmatched counts — including what ANPU did NOT detect.

.PP
The benchmark measures; it does not pass or fail. A completed measurement
always exits 0 (even with MISS verdicts). Freshness enforcement is opt-in
via --check, which CI uses to keep docs/benchmark.md honest.

.PP
Only point bench at targets you own or are explicitly authorized to test.
The local fixture (tests/bench) is the intended target:

.PP
docker compose -f tests/bench/docker-compose.yml up -d
  anpu bench --target http://127.0.0.1:8901


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--check\fP=""
	fail (exit 1) if this docs file's freshness section differs from measured output

.PP
\fB--format\fP="table"
	output format: table, json, or markdown

.PP
\fB--ground-truth\fP="tests/bench/ground-truth.yml"
	path to ground-truth.yml

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for bench

.PP
\fB--out\fP=""
	write output to a file instead of stdout

.PP
\fB--profiles\fP="safe,advanced"
	comma-separated scan profiles to measure

.PP
\fB--refresh-docs\fP=""
	replace the freshness section in this docs file and exit

.PP
\fB--runs\fP=1
	runs per profile (table shows run 1; JSON keeps all runs)

.PP
\fB--target\fP="http://127.0.0.1:8901"
	fixture target URL (only loopback targets get automatic local-network allowance)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBanpu(1)\fP


